const e="mansfield-festival-speech-drama",d=2026,a="Read the festival's two Speech & Drama class pages, both syllabus PDFs, the junior poems PDF, the three entry form PDFs, the Rules & Conditions of Entry page, the home page (FAQ, dates, contacts) and the Child Protection Policy. The template carries only Character Study and Duologue, so only those have competition rows; every other class family is named in one line under 'other'. Prices are in pounds (the pound sign is damaged on the web pages and read correctly in the PDFs). Older values kept here: the Primary & Junior PDF gives the festival as April 24th, 25th and 26th 2026 while the web pages give 23rd-25th April 2026 (newer web value used); the Senior & Adult PDF gives Duologue D33 as 4 minutes, D34 as 5 minutes and D35 as 7 minutes while the web page gives 3, 4 and 5 minutes (web used); the web Primary & Junior page lists D32 as 11 years and under while the Senior & Adult page lists it as 12 years and under (12 used, as the template does). Not copied: the festival's bank sort code and account number, the paper entry address (a house address) and the personal email printed on the entry forms. The festival's own bank transfer and cheque method is described in words. The Rules & Conditions page says no entries after the closing date; the FAQ says late entries are accepted but not in the programme. Both are recorded. Not printed: the venue of the Drama Festival (only the Music Festival venue and the Choirs Day venue are printed), the mark bands of the new marking scheme, and any team size for Duologue beyond the word duologue. A gift token donor named in the Bible reading class is not copied.",t=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Mansfield Music & Drama Festival 2026, Speech & Drama section. Read these rules before you enter.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Entering","Notice":"The Drama Festival is on {{DramaFestivalDates}}. The closing date for all entries is {{EntriesClosingDate}}. Enter online or send a paper entry form.","Notes":["Closing date for all entries: {{EntriesClosingDate}}.","Drama Festival: {{DramaFestivalDates}}.","Speech & Drama adjudicator: {{SpeechDramaAdjudicator}}.","Prize Winners Concert: {{PrizeWinnersConcert}}."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The festival was formed in 1924 as a festival of music, speech and drama in which people of all ages can perform as competitors or as non-competitors.","The festival is a registered charity (number 1039401) and is a member of the British and International Federation of Festivals.","A professional adjudicator gives each entrant a spoken and a written assessment.","The events take place over separate weekends in the spring, and a final concert is presented in which selected performers take part.","In 2026 the festival uses the new mark scheme of the British and International Federation of Festivals.","Parents and teachers are responsible for the safety of young people and their belongings during the festival. See the Child Protection Policy.","All school groups must be adequately supervised.","In the competition the decision of the adjudicator is final.","No competitor or member of the audience may approach the adjudicator during the session.","Competitors who do not answer to their number when called are called again at the end of the class.","A copy of every own choice item must be given to the adjudicator. Photocopies are kept by the festival and destroyed.","For own choice drama selections, send a copy of the script with your entry for the adjudicator.","Exact timing of own choice items is very important to the running of the programme. Competitors who go over the time limit are penalised. Keep to the stated times.","Entrants for improvisation classes should arrive at least 15 minutes before the class so that the adjudicator can give the subject.","For group acting classes, copies of the pieces should be sent with the entry if possible.","For devised drama classes, the theme or scenario must be given to the adjudicator before the class."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["People of all ages can enter, as competitors or as non-competitors.","Classes are for a school year group (for example Year 4 and under) or for an age (for example 12 years and under) or are Open, as printed for each class.","Character Study: one character only.","Character Study D61 is for Year 4 and under. D62 is for Year 6 and under. D63 is for Years 7 and 8. D64 is for Years 9 and 10. D65 is for Years 11 to 13. D66 is Open.","Duologue D31 is for 9 years and under. D32 is for 12 years and under. D33 is for 14 years and under. D34 is for 16 years and under. D35 is Open.","To enter without a mark, tick Non-competitive on the entry form. The entrant still receives an adjudication."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Enter online through the festival's online entry system, or complete a paper entry form and post it to the festival with your payment.","There are three Speech & Drama paper forms: Solos, Multiple Entrants in One Class, and Choral Verse.","On the form give the name as it should appear in the programme, a phone number, an email address, the class name and number, the piece title, the author and the duration.","On the form, agree to follow the Festival Rules and Regulations, and say yes or no to photographs by the official photographer.","The form is signed by the entrant, or by a parent or guardian if the entrant is under 18.","The multiple entrants form and the choral verse form are signed by the person in charge, with their position.","The closing date for all entries is {{EntriesClosingDate}}. The Rules and Conditions of Entry say no entries are accepted after this date.","The festival FAQ says late entries may be accepted, but the entrant's name will not be in the programme.","Entries are not acknowledged before the programme is made. If you need an acknowledgement, enclose a stamped addressed envelope.","A request for a specific day or time can be written on the entry form. The festival tries to meet it but cannot promise it.","Enter as many classes as you like."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and How to Pay","Items":["Character Study: {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}} for D61, D62, D63 and D64. {{CharacterStudyFeeOlder}} for D65 and D66.","Duologue: {{DuologueFeeJunior}} for D31, D32, D33 and D34. {{DuologueFeeOpen}} for D35.","All entries must be paid by cheque or by bank transfer into the festival bank account. Quote the entrant's name and the class when paying by bank transfer.","Make a cheque payable to the festival association and write the performer's name on the back. Send it with the entry form, or post it to the entry address if the form is emailed.","Using online banking helps keep the festival's banking charges down."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Important Dates","Items":["Drama Festival: {{DramaFestivalDates}}.","Closing date for all entries: {{EntriesClosingDate}}.","Prize Winners Concert: {{PrizeWinnersConcert}}."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Marks","Items":["A non-competitive entry receives no mark.","The festival uses the new marking scheme of the British and International Federation of Festivals in 2026.","The printed rules do not give the mark bands themselves."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Certificates, Trophies and Concert","Items":["Certificates are awarded to all competitors with 81 marks or more.","Small trophies or medals are awarded to competitors aged 16 and under. In other classes the adjudicator decides.","All trophies awarded at the Festival Concert are the property of the festival. They must be returned at least 4 weeks before the next festival. Phone {{DramaEnquiries}} for this.","Selected performers take part in the Prize Winners Concert on {{PrizeWinnersConcert}}."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct, Recording and Safeguarding","Items":["Under Performing Right Society rules, no performance may be recorded by tape, video or phone. No flash photography is allowed.","The award of certificates and trophies can be photographed with the permission of the child or children involved.","No unauthorised photography is allowed at festivals of the Federation. If a child, young person or parent is worried about photography or recording, they should speak to the Festival Safeguarding Officer.","All festival staff and volunteers wear a badge showing their role. Teachers, parents and carers are asked to report any incident to anyone wearing a festival badge. A quiet area is available where concerns can be raised in private.","During the festival, teachers, parents and carers are responsible for the continuous care and supervision of their own children or pupils. If they cannot attend, they must hand this to an identified adult and make sure the children know who that adult is. The festival takes no responsibility for property left unattended.","Children and adults who need support to take part: the responsible adult must contact the festival organisers before arriving. The festival tries to meet the need but must know beforehand, or will say that help cannot be given this time.","By signing the entry form, parents, guardians, carers and teachers of entrants under 18 (or of adults who need extra support) confirm they have given or obtained the consent needed for the entrant to take part. Without consent the entry cannot be accepted.","In relevant vocal classes the lyrics must be age appropriate for performers under 16."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging","Items":["Each class is judged by the festival's professional adjudicator: {{SpeechDramaAdjudicator}}.","The Festival Committee can re-grade pieces if appropriate."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Classes in the Syllabus","Items":["Verse Speaking and Own Choice Verse Speaking: set poems for Year 1 to Year 13 and own choice classes, including humorous verse. Poems for Years 1 to 6 are in the Junior Poems PDF, for rehearsal only and not to be reproduced.","Individual Reading: prepared prose, reading at sight, prose from memory, Bible reading and Bible from memory, group reading for 3 to 10 people, with set passages named in the syllabus.","Choral Verse Speaking: classes CS1 to CS4 for school year groups, with one set poem or an own choice poem.","Poetry Writing and Reading: original poems, written only, or written and read aloud. The Primary and Junior web page says a poem is no more than 26 lines and the PDFs say no more than 36 lines. Poems must be sent at least 3 weeks before the festival.","Art: class C1 is a picture inspired by a poem, for Years 1 to 6. Send a copy of the poem with the artwork.","Public Speaking: Show and Tell for Year 6 and under, and talks for Year 11 and under and Open.","Mime and Improvisation: original solo mime, solo improvisation, duologue improvisation and group improvisation.","Sonnet and Shakespeare classes: sonnet speaking, solo Shakespeare, Shakespeare duologue and a Shakespeare acting class.","Group Acting: one-act plays or devised drama for Year 6 and under, Years 7 and 8, Year 13 and under, and Open.","Performance Solos and Groups: acted scenes, performing arts solo and group, character study solo with song, original monologue, group speaking, and adult and child.","Gaining Experience classes (poem, reading, character study; ages 12 to 15, and Open) are open to anyone who has not won First prize at this festival. Senior Citizen classes (solo and group entertainment) are also listed. These classes can be competitive or non-competitive, and the entrant says which on the entry form.","Music section: piano, woodwind, brass, strings, small ensembles, vocal, choirs and bands. Music Festival: {{MusicFestivalDates}} at {{MusicVenue}}. Choirs Day and Bands: {{ChoirsDay}}. Music rules about grade bands: enter the grade you have just taken or are preparing to take, not a grade below, and enter only one grade band for an instrument."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Primary & Junior Speech & Drama syllabus 2026 (PDF)","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/PMMDFPrimaryJuniorsyllabus26.pdf"},{"Title":"Senior & Adult Speech & Drama syllabus 2026 (PDF)","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/MMDFSenior-0AdultSyllabus2026.pdf"},{"Title":"Junior poems 2026 (PDF)","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/MMDF-Junior-poems-2026.pdf"},{"Title":"Entry form: Solos Speech & Drama (PDF)","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Solo_Speech_-_Drama.pdf"},{"Title":"Entry form: Multiple Entrants in One Class (PDF)","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Drama_Multiple_Entrants.pdf"},{"Title":"Entry form: Choral Verse (PDF)","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Choral_Verse_Entry_Form.pdf"},{"Title":"Online entry system","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.runmyfestival.net/runMyFestival/security/welcome.jsf"},{"Title":"Rules & Conditions of Entry","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/rules-conditions-of-entry/"},{"Title":"Child Protection Policy (PDF)","Url":"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Child_Protection_Policy_.pdf"},{"Title":"New BIFF marking scheme","Url":"https://www.federationoffestivals.org.uk/new-biff-marking-scheme-2024"}]}`),r=[],n=[],s=[{Title:"Character Study",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Primary & Junior 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF); Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF), Character Study",Sections:{About:["One character only."],TimeAndFormat:["D61: Year 4 and under, time limit 2 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}}.","D62: Year 6 and under, time limit 3 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}}.","D63: Years 7 and 8, own choice, time limit 4 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}}.","D64: Years 9 and 10, own choice, time limit 4 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}}.","D65: Years 11 to 13, own choice, time limit 5 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeOlder}}.","D66: Open, own choice, time limit 6 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeOlder}}."],Rules:["For own choice pieces a copy must be given to the adjudicator."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["Competitors who go over the time limit are penalised."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- One character only.

## Time and format
- D61: Year 4 and under, time limit 2 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}}.
- D62: Year 6 and under, time limit 3 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}}.
- D63: Years 7 and 8, own choice, time limit 4 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}}.
- D64: Years 9 and 10, own choice, time limit 4 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeYoung}}.
- D65: Years 11 to 13, own choice, time limit 5 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeOlder}}.
- D66: Open, own choice, time limit 6 minutes, entry fee {{CharacterStudyFeeOlder}}.

## Rules
- For own choice pieces a copy must be given to the adjudicator.

## Notes for participants
- Competitors who go over the time limit are penalised.`},{Title:"Duologue",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Primary & Junior 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF); Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF), Duologues",Sections:{About:["Two performers. Own choice."],TimeAndFormat:["D31: 9 years and under, time limit 3 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeJunior}}.","D32: 12 years and under, time limit 4 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeJunior}}.","D33: 14 years and under, time limit 3 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeJunior}}.","D34: 16 years and under, time limit 4 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeJunior}}.","D35: Open, time limit 5 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeOpen}}."],Rules:["A copy of the piece must be given to the adjudicator."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["Competitors who go over the time limit are penalised."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Two performers. Own choice.

## Time and format
- D31: 9 years and under, time limit 3 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeJunior}}.
- D32: 12 years and under, time limit 4 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeJunior}}.
- D33: 14 years and under, time limit 3 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeJunior}}.
- D34: 16 years and under, time limit 4 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeJunior}}.
- D35: Open, time limit 5 minutes, entry fee {{DuologueFeeOpen}}.

## Rules
- A copy of the piece must be given to the adjudicator.

## Notes for participants
- Competitors who go over the time limit are penalised.`}],o=[{Title:"Character Study",AgeGroup:"15-16",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF), D65",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["Shakespeare is not allowed in this class (D65, Years 11 to 13)."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Not allowed
- Shakespeare is not allowed in this class (D65, Years 11 to 13).`},{Title:"Character Study",AgeGroup:"16-18",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF), D65",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["Shakespeare is not allowed in this class (D65, Years 11 to 13)."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Not allowed
- Shakespeare is not allowed in this class (D65, Years 11 to 13).`}],i=[{Key:"DramaFestivalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Drama Festival dates",Value:"23rd-25th April 2026",Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"},{Key:"EntriesClosingDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Closing date for all entries",Value:"2026-02-28",Source:"Rules & Conditions of Entry (festival web page); Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"},{Key:"PrizeWinnersConcert",Kind:"date",Label:"Prize Winners Concert",Value:"Sunday 10th May 2026 at The Palace Theatre, Mansfield",Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"},{Key:"MusicFestivalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Music Festival dates",Value:"25th-26th April 2026",Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"},{Key:"ChoirsDay",Kind:"date",Label:"Choirs Day and Bands",Value:"27th April 2026 at The Palace Theatre, Mansfield NG18 1NG",Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"},{Key:"MusicVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Music Festival venue",Value:{Name:"Crescent Centre",Address:"Peel Crescent",City:"Mansfield NG19 7LW",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"},{Key:"SpeechDramaAdjudicator",Kind:"text",Label:"Speech & Drama adjudicator",Value:"Susan Mackay",Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"},{Key:"CharacterStudyFeeYoung",Kind:"fee",Label:"Character Study fee, Years 4 to 10 (D61-D64)",Value:"4.00 pounds per entry",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Primary & Junior 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF); Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF)"},{Key:"CharacterStudyFeeOlder",Kind:"fee",Label:"Character Study fee, Years 11-13 and Open (D65, D66)",Value:"5.00 pounds per entry",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF)"},{Key:"DuologueFeeJunior",Kind:"fee",Label:"Duologue fee, 16 years and under (D31-D34)",Value:"7.50 pounds per entry",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Primary & Junior 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF); Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF)"},{Key:"DuologueFeeOpen",Kind:"fee",Label:"Duologue fee, Open (D35)",Value:"8.50 pounds per entry",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF)"},{Key:"DramaEnquiries",Kind:"contact",Label:"Drama enquiries",Value:{Name:"Drama enquiries",Role:"Mansfield Music & Drama Festival",Phone:"01623 627636",WhatsApp:"",Email:"drama@mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk"},Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"},{Key:"GeneralEnquiries",Kind:"contact",Label:"General festival email",Value:{Name:"Festival",Role:"General enquiries",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"info@mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk"},Source:"Festival website header"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed on the festival site",Value:[{Date:"",Title:"New mark scheme in 2026",Text:"In 2026 the festival uses the new mark scheme of the British and International Federation of Festivals.",Url:"https://www.federationoffestivals.org.uk/new-biff-marking-scheme-2024"},{Date:"2026-05-10",Title:"Prize Winners Concert",Text:"The Prize Winners Concert is on Sunday 10th May 2026 at The Palace Theatre, Mansfield.",Url:""}],Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)"}],l=[{Claim:"Classes, time limits and fees for Character Study and Duologue.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own class pages and syllabus PDFs",Source:"Speech & Drama Classes - Primary & Junior 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF); Speech & Drama Classes - Senior & Adult 2026 (web page and syllabus PDF)",Url:"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/speech-drama-classes-senior-adult/"},{Claim:"Rules, closing date, certificates and recording rules.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own rules page",Source:"Rules & Conditions of Entry (festival web page)",Url:"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/rules-conditions-of-entry/"},{Claim:"Festival dates, adjudicator, contacts, FAQ and concert.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own home page",Source:"Festival home page 2026 (dates, FAQ, contacts)",Url:"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/"},{Claim:"Entry form contents and signing rules.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own entry forms",Source:"Entry Forms page and the three Speech & Drama entry form PDFs",Url:"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/entry-forms/"},{Claim:"Safeguarding rules.",SourceType:"Primary - Federation Child Protection Policy published by the festival",Source:"Child Protection Policy PDF (Creating Safer Festivals for Everyone)",Url:"https://mansfieldmusicdramafestival.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Child_Protection_Policy_.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:a,Page:t,ParticipantTypes:r,AgeGroups:n,Competitions:s,CompetitionAgeGroups:o,Variables:i,Evidence:l};export{n as AgeGroups,o as CompetitionAgeGroups,s as Competitions,l as Evidence,a as Note,t as Page,r as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,i as Variables,d as Year,u as default};
